.TH SIG 3
.SH NAME
sig \- signal interface routines
.SH SYNOPSIS
.nf
.ft CR
#include <ast.h>
#include <sig.h>

Sig_handler_t  signal(int \fIsig\fP, Sig_handler_t \fIhandler\fP);
int            sigcritical(int \fIop\fP);
int            sigflag(int \fIsig\fP, int \fIflags\fP, int \fIset\fP);
int            sigunblock(int \fIsig\fP);
.ft
.fi
.SH DESCRIPTION
These routines provide a portable interface to signal handling.
.PP
\f[CB]signal\fP
installs
.I handler
for the signal
.I sig
using
.IR sigaction (2)
and returns the previous handler.
Unlike the standard
.IR signal (3),
the restart semantics are controlled per signal: slow system calls are
restarted for
.BR SIGIO ,
.BR SIGTSTP ,
.BR SIGTTIN
and
.BR SIGTTOU
and interrupted
.RB ( EINTR )
for the other signals.
If
.I handler
is
.B SIG_DFL
then the signal is also unblocked via
\f[CB]sigunblock\fP;
this is suppressed if
.I sig
is negative, in which case
.I \-sig
is used.
.PP
\f[CB]sigunblock\fP
is called to
unblock the signal
.I sig
from within a handler currently servicing
.IR sig .
If
.I sig
is 0 then all signals are unblocked.
0 is returned on success, \-1 on error.
.PP
\f[CB]sigflag\fP
sets
.RI ( "set != 0" )
or clears
.RI ( "set == 0" )
the
.I flags
bits in the
.IR sigaction (2)
.I sa_flags
for the signal
.IR sig .
0 is returned on success, \-1 on error.
.PP
\f[CB]sigcritical\fP
controls a critical region for a set of signals selected by the
inclusive-or of the following
.I op
flags:
.TP
\f[CB]SIG_REG_EXEC\fP
.BR SIGINT ,
.BR SIGPIPE ,
.BR SIGQUIT
and
.B SIGHUP
are held.
.TP
\f[CB]SIG_REG_PROC\fP
.B SIGCHLD
is held.
.TP
\f[CB]SIG_REG_TERM\fP
.BR SIGTSTP ,
.BR SIGTTIN
and
.B SIGTTOU
are held.
.TP
\f[CB]SIG_REG_ALL\fP
All of the above signals are held.
.TP
\f[CB]SIG_REG_SET\fP
The region signals are set without incrementing the region nesting level.
.PP
.B "op > 0"
pushes the region (blocking the selected signals),
.B "op == 0"
(\f[CB]SIG_REG_POP\fP)
pops the region (restoring the previous signal mask), and
.B "op < 0"
(\f[CB]SIG_REG_PENDING\fP)
returns non-zero if any of the region signals are being held pending in the
current critical region.
Signal critical regions may be nested.
The current critical region level is returned for
.BR "op >= 0" ,
.B \-1
on error.
.PP
The global variable
.nf
.ft CR
Sig_info_t sig_info;
.ft
.fi
contains the signal name and description tables:
.I sig_info.name[\fIsig\fP]
is the signal name sans
\f[CB]SIG\fP
and
.I sig_info.text[\fIsig\fP]
is the signal description text, for signal numbers up to
.IR sig_info.sigmax .
.SH "SEE ALSO"
.IR signal (2),
.IR sigaction (2)
